WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.180
Even though it’s already three hours long,
not all of Avengers: Endgame made it to the

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:05.680
screen.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.960
Some of the deleted scenes are probably best
left on the cutting room floor, while others

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.600
might've made the movie even better.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.160
From goji berries to a tearful farewell, here
are the scenes you didn't get to see.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:22.140
One of the six deleted Avengers: Endgame scenes
is ordinary but unintentionally hilarious

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.080
for a few reasons.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.320
Titled "Goji Berries," the moment takes us
inside Pepper Potts and Tony Stark's lakeside

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.780
cabin, where they're living in married bliss
and discussing fairly unexciting things...like

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.780
alpacas and berries.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.860
"First of all, Gerald is our alpaca."

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.860
"He's not my alpaca if he's eating my gojis."

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.420
"Okay, they're gonna be nice in the salad
right there."

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:41.920
"No, don't!

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:42.420
Don't!

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:42.920
Don't!

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.920
The scene is extra humorous considering Paltrow's
real-life love of health, wellness, and cooking.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.540
As some Marvel fans may know, Paltrow owns
the natural health company Goop, which sells

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.120
clothes, shoes, supplements, and yes, even
goji berries.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.760
Another deleted Avengers: Endgame scene references
the events at the end of Captain America:

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.680
The First Avenger.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:08.000
Bearing the title "Bombs on Board," the sequence
features James "Rhodey" Rhodes and Steve Rogers

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.131
running through what happened to the Tesseract
after Cap crashed a Hydra aircraft in The

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:12.980
First Avenger.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.040
The Tesseract, which the present-day Avengers
were looking to find as part of their time

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.920
heist mission, fell out of the plane and sank
to the bottom of the ocean during the crash.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.580
"Why did you have to crash the plane, anyway?"

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.060
"Bombs on board."

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.760
So Rhodey asks the obvious question:

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.660
"And you couldn't have jumped out of the plane
before you crashed it?"

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.220
Seriously, why didn't he jump out?

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.100
That's one moment where Rogers could take
a good, hard look at his past self and say...

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.320
"That is America's ass."

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:54.040
A silly and unfinished scene cut from the
theatrical version of Avengers: Endgame features

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.720
Rocket Raccoon sitting with surviving members
of the Avengers crew at the team's headquarters.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:03.000
Gathered around a table, the heroes watch
some footage from the Avengers' fight against

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.640
the Chitauri in the 2012 Battle of New York,
as seen in the first Avengers film.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.390
Rocket asks how long Earth's Mightiest Heroes
fought, and Black Widow responds, "About two,

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.180
two or three hours."

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.450
The snarky raccoon is shocked that the Avengers
spent that much time in battle with the aliens.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.280
"The Chitauri are the suckiest army in the
galaxy.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.180
Why didn't you just blow up the mothership?"

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.670
Rocket gets a good laugh out of how inept
the Avengers were, but, of course, Tony Stark

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.160
always gets the last laugh.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.220
"You didn't know that was a thing?

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.260
Everyone knows…"

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.940
In another deleted scene that still has some
early CGI, Rocket and Thor in his "Fat Thor"

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:46.720
state are back in the year 2013, lurking through
the halls of the Asgardian Palace.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.920
The two are trying to determine which path
to take to avoid the Dark Elves' attack and

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.170
retrieve the Reality Stone to take back to
2023.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.620
Unfortunately, the god of thunder is of little
help when Rocket asks which way to go.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:03.480
After urinating off the side of a palace wall
to the floor below, Thor says that he's not

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.660
coping well with being back in Asgard during
the time in which he witnessed so much death.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.200
He admits he doesn't know the correct path
to safety, but Rocket doesn't appreciate the

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:12.700
honesty.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.260
"You used to frickin' live here!"

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.200
"For 1,500 years, not forever.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.260
That way I think.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:18.760
Yeah, maybe."

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:19.740
"We are dead.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.340
We are so, so dead."

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:26.020
The scenes between Tony Stark and his distant
father Howard Stark were some of the most

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.860
heartwarming ones in Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:33.020
However, a small moment left out of the final
film would have inspired even more fuzzy feelings.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.660
As the father-son duo are walking through
the 1970s S.H.I.E.L.D. base while discussing

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:42.001
the fears that come with first-time fatherhood
and the importance of leaving a legacy, Howard

00:03:42.001 --> 00:03:44.620
gives Tony an offer that must have been hard
to refuse.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.640
But Tony doesn't miss a beat with his reply.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.440
"You wanna come work for me, Potts?"

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.300
"I'm a little tied up in futures right now."

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.260
Get it?

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:55.360
Because he's from the future?

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.780
Anyway, it's a brief little moment, but we'll
take all the Stark family bonding we can get.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:07.040
"Thank you for everything you've done for
this country."

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:12.320
While the rest of the deleted Avengers: Endgame
scenes are all under a minute long, the final

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.280
one comes in at almost two minutes.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:19.211
The heftiest sequence both in terms of emotion
and length, the "Avengers Take a Knee" scene

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:24.120
happens immediately after Tony Stark sacrifices
his life in the battle against Thanos.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:29.160
As Tony slips away, Pepper Potts kisses his
cheek while the Avengers look on and realize

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.760
the weight of what just happened.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:35.680
Hawkeye drops to one knee and places his head
against his hand to honor the fallen Avenger

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.760
who started the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.720
This sparks a chain reaction, and one by one
the rest of the heroes kneel in respect.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:48.060
We even catch a shot of the 2014 Gamora looking
on, almost contemplating kneeling before turning

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.020
and walking away.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.400
Maybe she's going to hang out with Deadpool
in the non-kneeling clubhouse.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.900
"You know, that's really hard on your knees.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:55.910
Totally impractical.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:56.400
They all do it."

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:01.640
This deleted scene is impactful, but let's
be honest: the theatrical scene was already

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:02.520
heartbreaking enough.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:07.460
Adding this into the mix would have left everyone
full-on sobbing into their popcorn.

